Franjo Kalanj||son of Viol Kalanj and Kate Zoričić, of Brinje - a sibling of Kate Kalanj, this file - not in the tree|baptism|10 August 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 218, entry no. 76 - "KALANJ FRANJO", male, of Brinje house 189, son of KALANJ VIOL and ZORIČIĆ KATE. NOT IN THE TREE. The same parents already in this file as Viol Kalanj and Zoričić Kate, whose daughter Kate was born December 1890 - confirming a second child and a real household, not a single register entry. The house number here, 189, does not match the 118 recorded for that earlier birth; whether the family moved, or one of the two numbers was misread, is not established.
Niko Hofjenc, son of Niko Hofjenc and Marija Borić||son of Niko Hofjenc and Marija Borić, of Brinje - not in the tree|baptism|11 October 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 227, entry no. 113 - "HOFJENC NIKO", male, of Brinje, son of HOFJENC NIKO and BORIĆ MARIJA. A witness on the same entry is again "BORIĆ MARIJA", alongside Draženović Ive. NOT IN THE TREE. This confirms the marriage already in this file from the Vjenčani book (image 564): Marija Borić, spinster, 19, of Brinje house 142, daughter of Niko Borić, married Hofjenc Niko around 1892-93. A child within about a year is exactly the timeline that marriage implies - the first direct confirmation the marriage actually took place and produced a family. The witness sharing her exact name is left unexplained: possibly the mother herself entered twice, possibly a second Marija Borić, not established.
Luce Borić, daughter of Tome Borić||daughter of Tome Borić, of Kamenica house 24 - not in the tree|baptism|18 October 1893|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 229, entry no. 120 - "BORIĆ LUCE", female, of Kamenica house 24, daughter of BORIĆ TOME and RADOTIĆ MARIJA. NOT IN THE TREE. A third birth at Kamenica house 24 in this file, after Marija Borić (married out 1897, father recorded as Niko Borić and Bare) and Kate Borić (born 1893, father Niko Borić and Radotić Dace) - but this child's father is entered as Tome, not Niko, and her mother as Radotić Marija, not Radotić Dace. Whether Tome is Niko's brother sharing the house, a second Borić household at the same number, or a scribal slip on the father's name is not established; kept as a separate person, not merged.
Anica Kalanj||daughter of Niko Kalanj and Marija Vučetić, of Brinje house 231 - not in the tree|baptism|21 August 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 235, entry no. 144 - "KALANJ ANICA" [given name partly worn, read with reasonable confidence], female, of Brinje house 231, daughter of KALANJ NIKO and VUČETIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Vuković Stjepan and Vučetić Janja. NOT IN THE TREE. This is very likely the first confirmed child of Niko Kalanj, already the very first Kalanj household this archive found at Brinje (Vjenčani book, image 530: Niko Kalanj, bachelor, 40, son of Juro Kalanj, married a widow named Marija, 33, in 1890). The mother's maiden name here, Vučetić, matches cleanly with no contradiction - unlike the Kamenica house 24 puzzle elsewhere in this file, this is a clean confirmation that the marriage produced a household.
Kate Borić, witness at Brinje house 85||witness to the baptism of Javor Frica, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|24 December 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 239, entry no. 159 - the baptism of "JAVOR FRICA", female, of Brinje house 85, daughter of Javor Ivan and Đorić Kate, names "BORIĆ KATE" as a witness alongside Jelačić Stjepan. NOT IN THE TREE. A witness only, no house number of her own given. Kept separate from the other women named Kate Borić already in this file; nothing ties them together.
Grgo Borić, witness at Brinje house 74||witness to the baptism of Milaković Marko, of Brinje - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|24 December 1893|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 239, entry no. 160 - the baptism of "MILAKOVIĆ MARKO", male, of Brinje house 74, son of Milaković Marko and Milaković Kate, names "BORIĆ GRGO" as a witness alongside Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. A plausible match, not a confirmed one, for the Grgo Borić already in this file as father of Stjepan Borić at Brinje house 126 (born August 1893, four months earlier) - the same given name in the same parish in the same year, but no document names them as the same man.
Ove Borić, daughter of Tome Borić||daughter of Tome Borić and Jela Borić, of Brinje house 141 - a fourth sibling alongside Juraj, Petar and Matija Borić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|10 January 1894|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 242, entry no. 9 - "BORIĆ OVE", female, born 10 January 1894 and registered the next day, of Brinje house 141, daughter of BORIĆ TOME and BORIĆ JELE. Witnesses Perkić Mijo i Kate (the recurring near-miss surname, distinct from Perković). NOT IN THE TREE. A FOURTH CHILD of the same Borić-marries-Borić household already in this file (Juraj, 1888; Petar, 1890; Matija, 1892) - the same house number and both parents' names, this time with no discrepancy in the mother's name. Kept separate from the Ove Borić already in this file (wife of Ivan Javor, house 41, a mother by 1891) - different generation, different house, no document ties them.
Luce Borić, daughter of Lojze Borić||daughter of Lojze Borić, of Kamenica house 83 - not in the tree|baptism|6 February 1894|Kamenica, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 244, entry no. 17 - "BORIĆ LUCE", female, born 6 February 1894, of Kamenica house 83, daughter of BORIĆ LOJZE and MESIĆ MANDA-MARIJA (the mother's given name entered with what reads as two names or a correction). Witnesses Škorup Ivo i Marija. A later hand added a civil-era annotation in the margin, not transcribed here. NOT IN THE TREE. A new Borić given name (Lojze) at a new Kamenica house number (83), distinct from the already-puzzling Kamenica house 24 - kept separate, no document ties this household to any other Borić in this file. A fourth person in this file named Luce Borić; nothing ties her to the other three (Brinje house 126, Kamenica unmarried mother, Kamenica house 24 daughter of Tome).
