Ana Borić, daughter of Grgo Borić||daughter of Grgo Borić and Marija Milaković, of Brinje house 126 - a sibling of Stjepan Borić, this file - not in the tree|baptism|25 December 1894|Brinje, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 278, entry no. 153 - "BORIĆ ANA", female, born 25 December 1894, of Brinje house 126, daughter of BORIĆ GRGO and MILAKOVIĆ MARIJA. Witnesses Dražičević Mile i Kate. NOT IN THE TREE. A SECOND CHILD of the same household already in this file (Stjepan Borić, born August 1893, image 203) - the same house number and both parents' names, confirming Grgo Borić and Marija Milaković as a real, continuing household at house 126, not a single register entry. Whether this Grgo is the same man as Ivan/Ive Borić, whose children Juko and Luce were also tied to house 126, remains not established.
Ivan Borić, witness at Lučane||witness to the baptism of Lovinčić Ove, of Lučane - not in the tree|witness at a baptism|27 December 1894|Lučane, Brinje parish, Croatia|FamilySearch, Croatia Church Books 1516-1994, Brinje Matična knjiga rođenih 1893-1897 (DGS 005498262, waypoint 9R26-82S), image 279, entry no. 1 - the baptism of "LOVINČIĆ OVE", male, of Lučane house 28, son of Lovinčić Tome and Lovinčić Kate, names "BORIĆ IVAN" as a witness alongside Marija. NOT IN THE TREE. The first Borić name this file has placed at Lučane as a witness (a Borić woman, Ove, already married out to a Lučane household in 1893) - kept separate from the several other Borić men already named Ivan/Ive in this file, since nothing here ties him to any of them.
